
  IPSEITY · the tokens talking

  a collection, and a place to talk
  ✓ the parley is deployed
  ✓ two tokens, two holders
  ✓ the contract derives the same topic the events carry

  the commons, written across several blocks
  ✓ every message came back
  ✓ in the order they were said
  ✓ and each is attributed to the token that said it
  ✓ the sequence numbers are the room's, not the block's
  ✓ and it took one query per block that had a message, not one per block
      405 blocks of history, read in 3 single-block queries
  ✓ two messages in one block do not send the walk in a circle
  ✓ and following the newest log instead would have looped, which is why it does not
      (the walk follows the oldest log in a block, which is why it terminates)

  a message is signed by the token, not by an address
  ✓ a wallet cannot speak as a token it does not hold
  ✓ but the token's own account may speak for it
  ✓ and a renter may not

  two tokens, one room, derived rather than founded
  ✓ the key is the same from both sides
  ✓ both halves of the conversation are in it
  ✓ and it reads in order
  ✓ the commons did not gain them
  ✓ and the raw key is not a door into it

  a group
  ✓ the first group takes the first key
  ✓ and it is a group
  ✓ with one member
  ✓ and a steward
  ✓ a closed door stays closed
  ✓ and nothing was added to the uninvited token's list
  ✓ an invitation alone still adds nothing to it
  ✓ joining is what adds it, and only the token can join
  ✓ the group has its own archive
  ✓ kept apart from every other room's

  a body is bytes, and stays the bytes it was
  ✓ a body that is markup comes back as the same characters
  ✓ byte for byte
      (what stops it being markup is the client, and that is checked in verify-site)
  ✓ a sealed body is flagged rather than interpreted
  ✓ a body over 1024 bytes is refused

  polling is one call and two numbers
  ✓ three rooms in, three counts out
  ✓ the commons count
  ✓ the group count
  ✓ the pair count
  ✓ and a head block for each

  37 passed, 0 failed
